I can handle this. There's supposed to be some air on the deck, right? If I can breathe, there's no problem.

259
00:18:47,227 --> 00:18:54,227
Deccan needs the bubble. That much is true. However, Horty may still destroy it if worse comes to worse.

260
00:18:54,227 --> 00:19:02,227
Take this baby transponder snail. This will be our last resort in the event that things go poorly. We must be prepared for anything.

261
00:19:05,227 --> 00:19:08,227
Oh, Luffy. I don't know what to do!

262
00:19:08,227 --> 00:19:15,227
My brother told me that I should protect you and stay close to the Noah at any cost. But I don't understand what good that will do us now!

263
00:19:15,227 --> 00:19:18,227
Hang on. I think I know.

264
00:19:19,227 --> 00:19:23,227
Hey guys! What do we need to do to get a little air from you?

265
00:19:23,227 --> 00:19:26,227
We can shoot out all the air in the air tank.

266
00:19:26,227 --> 00:19:28,227
What is that thing for, anyway?

267
00:19:28,227 --> 00:19:37,227
It's an air conditioning facility that provides air for Fishman Island. If we create a big bubble and shoot it, maybe it'll surround the Noah.

268
00:19:37,227 --> 00:19:45,227
However, the bubble would neutralize ascending forces, so it's not going to make the Noah stop or reverse course.

269
00:19:45,227 --> 00:19:53,227
On top of that, we'd have to use all the air we've got to make the bubble big enough to hold the ship. And it would crash long before we could resupply.

270
00:19:53,227 --> 00:20:04,227
What I mean is we've got only one chance. If we don't manage to send out the bubble at the exact moment the Noah moves closest to the air tank, then we're done. It's over.

271
00:20:05,227 --> 00:20:08,227
All riding on one shot, huh? Wow. Better not miss.

272
00:20:08,227 --> 00:20:15,227
Right. I'm afraid that's all we can do. After we deploy the bubble, the rest is up to you. I should reiterate, this is-

273
00:20:15,227 --> 00:20:20,227
Don't make it more complicated. Just go for it, okay? If I can breathe, I'll make this work.

274
00:20:20,227 --> 00:20:27,227
All right, roger that. We'll do our best not to miss the ship. And Luffy, everyone here is counting on you.

275
00:20:28,227 --> 00:20:36,227
They're swimming alongside it. You're just a lowly human and a cowardly mermaid. What can you two possibly hope to accomplish now?

276
00:20:37,227 --> 00:20:39,227
Shark Tracer!

277
00:20:40,227 --> 00:20:42,227
Out of my way.

278
00:20:45,227 --> 00:20:47,227
Gormon Harsing!

279
00:20:50,227 --> 00:20:52,227
Out of my way.

280
00:21:20,227 --> 00:21:29,587
No way, he got even bigger?

281
00:21:33,647 --> 00:21:35,007
Ready to give up.

282
00:21:36,287 --> 00:21:38,367
You should be human.

283
00:21:39,287 --> 00:21:42,567
Just the sight of you vile worms makes me sick to my stomach.

284
00:21:43,447 --> 00:21:48,947
Even if it shortens my life and even if I have to sacrifice everything in this world.

285
00:21:48,947 --> 00:21:54,147
I swear to you, I will have my revenge against the human race.

286
00:21:55,187 --> 00:21:55,787
Hordy!

287
00:22:07,787 --> 00:22:11,027
You've only got one shot, so you better not miss it.

288
00:22:11,367 --> 00:22:13,807
If this doesn't work, the whole island's done for.

289
00:22:18,947 --> 00:22:21,847
Can you hear me, Straw Hat?

290
00:22:22,487 --> 00:22:24,387
Oh dear, that's my brother's voice!

291
00:22:24,387 --> 00:22:26,447
Hey buddy, are you okay?

292
00:22:31,567 --> 00:22:35,087
I'm barely alive, but please listen.

293
00:22:37,387 --> 00:22:40,387
He spoke earlier and...

294
00:22:43,807 --> 00:22:48,387
It's clear now. Hordy is...

295
00:22:48,947 --> 00:23:01,567
...

296
00:23:01,567 --> 00:23:14,327
The Straw Hats continue their battle with the new Fishman Pirates, having faith that Luffy will carry out his mission.

297
00:23:14,327 --> 00:23:16,727
Neptune's army aids them in the struggle,

298
00:23:16,727 --> 00:23:18,927
finally accepting the crew as allies.

299
00:23:18,927 --> 00:23:22,327
As the fight continues, Fukuboshi's transponder snail

300
00:23:22,327 --> 00:23:25,127
reveals the sober truth behind Horty's motivations

301
00:23:25,127 --> 00:23:26,927
to all of Fishman Island.

302
00:23:26,927 --> 00:23:30,227
On the next One Piece, a shocking fact,

303
00:23:30,227 --> 00:23:32,427
the true identity of Horty,

304
00:23:32,427 --> 00:23:34,927
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

